#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "A pass at the bar credits the chart's full level, the same as passing the course, and so does the first point above it: a 96.9% on a 96% ladder is a normal clear, not a bonus. Above that the bonus stays small until 99%, then it climbs. Under the bar a pass still counts, as a clear of a lower level, down to a level and a quarter less at the cutoff. Regular ladders credit to 4 points under the bar and 6K/7K LN to 1. 4K LN uses its own numbers: it credits down to 94.5%, a level and a half less there, and its bonus tops out at 99.7%:"
#~ msgstr "A pass at the bar credits the chart's full level, the same as passing the course, and so does the first point above it: a 96.9% on a 96% ladder is a normal clear, not a bonus. Above that the bonus stays small until 99%, then it climbs. Under the bar a pass still counts, as a clear of a lower level, down to a level and a quarter less at the cutoff. Regular ladders credit to 4 points under the bar and 6K/7K LN to 1. 4K LN uses its own numbers: it credits down to 94.5%, a level and a half less there, and its bonus tops out at 99.7%:"

#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
msgid "A pass has to be on one of these difficulties, or on another upload of one with the same notes, OD and HP; a cut or edited reupload does not count. REFORM's three INTRO courses and the 0th to 2nd of Jinjin's LN Phase I are left out, because they sit below the first level their ladder measures."
msgstr "A pass has to be on one of these difficulties, or on another upload of one with the same notes, OD and HP; a cut or edited reupload does not count. REFORM's three INTRO courses and the 0th to 2nd of Jinjin's LN Phase I are left out, because they sit below the first level their ladder measures."

